# Downloadable files

When the user asks for a file (zip, txt, xml, pdf, image, installer, or any other artifact they should take with them), **that turn is not done until they can download it**.

1. Copy the file to `/opt/cursor/artifacts/<filename>` (Cursor download tray).
2. Commit a copy under repo-root `patches/<filename>` (same pattern as InPmnt-PHP.zip) and push.
3. In the reply, lead with clickable downloads — never a VM path alone:
   - GitHub: `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/devildog5x5/InPmnt/<branch>/patches/<filename>`
   - Tray: `<a href="/opt/cursor/artifacts/<filename>">Download <filename></a>`
4. If you built more than one file, make **every** one downloadable the same way.
5. Prefer a **versioned** filename (`FamilyShieldPro-1.0.0.zip`) plus a latest alias (`FamilyShieldPro.zip`).
6. Do not say “it’s on the server” or “it’s in artifacts” without those two links.
